Biological Wastewater Treatment — Chen and colleagues, second edition (@wu-chen: 0, is #reference, #part-of @wu-sources) { r_1AE9DK0YWQR5GDECZ9KK1JJP37
Guanghao Chen, Mark C. M. van Loosdrecht, George A. Ekama and Damir Brdjanovic, editors. Biological Wastewater Treatment: Principles, Modelling and Design, second edition. [Publisher and chapters](https://iwaponline.com/ebooks/book/791/Biological-Wastewater-TreatmentPrinciples) · [DOI](https://doi.org/10.2166/9781789060362).

Work the whole eighteen-chapter progression after the introductory wastewater books. Follow metabolism and wastewater fractions through organic, nitrogen and phosphorus removal, aeration, settling, granules, membranes, models, control, anaerobic processes and biofilms. Use chapter-specific assumptions when moving between stoichiometric, kinetic and transport models.

The publisher identifies copyright 2020 and a July 2023 publication entry for this edition; these dates should not be collapsed into a new scientific edition. The indexed publisher page supplies the contents and a CC BY-NC-ND 4.0 notice, with third-party exceptions. Direct automated retrieval returned 403, so complete text inspection is not claimed. Consult the publisher's actual download and notices; open access does not authorize adapted copies under a no-derivatives licence.

